<title>USA: CarrAmerica sells $275 mln in 2-part deal.</title>
<headline>CarrAmerica sells $275 mln in 2-part deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche 144A debt deal from CarrAmerica Realty was priced on Thursday via JP Morgan Securities Inc, according to a syndicate official.</p>
<p>BORROWER  CARRAMERICA REALTY</p>
<p>AMT $150 MLN	 COUPON 7.20 PCT   MATURITY 7/1/2004</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.735  FIRST PAY DATE 1/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA3  YIELD 7.249 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB	 SPREAD 78 BPS     CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>AMT $125 MLN	 COUPON 7.375 PCT  MATURITY 7/1/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.672  FIRST PAY DATE 1/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA3  YIELD 7.422 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB	 SPREAD 93 BPS     CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>NOTE: The $150 million in notes were priced at a spread of 78 basis points over the blend.</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678 ))</p>
</text>
